{"kind": "chat_performance", "workload": "explanation", "repeat": 2, "prompt": "Explain how hash tables handle collisions, resizing, and adversarial input. Compare separate chaining with open addressing and give practical examples.", "input_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 814, 20139, 1204, 5010, 12269, 3579, 45776, 11, 83264, 11, 321, 27483, 41306, 1879, 13, 23024, 8387, 71159, 440, 1724, 26153, 321, 2873, 14542, 9989, 13, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 271, 248069, 271], "prompt_tokens": 38, "output_tokens": 256, "answer": "Hash tables are fundamental data structures that map keys to values using a hash function. However, because the range of possible keys is usually much larger than the size of the underlying array, **collisions** (two different keys hashing to the same index) are inevitable.\n\nBelow is a detailed explanation of how hash tables handle collisions, resizing, and adversarial input, followed a comparison of the two main collision resolution strategies: **Separate Chaining** and **Open Addressing**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Handling Collisions\n\nWhen two keys hash to the same index, the hash table must resolve the conflict. There are two primary strategies:\n\n#### A. Separate Chaining\n- **Mechanism**: Each bucket in the hash table array points to a linked list (or another dynamic data structure like a balanced tree).\n- **Collision Resolution**: When a collision occurs, the new key-value pair is simply added to the list at that bucket.\n- **Pros**:\n  - Simple to implement.\n  - Handles high load factors well (performance degrades gracefully).\n  - No need to resize immediately when the table fills up (though resizing is still needed for performance).\n- **Cons**:\n  - Extra memory overhead for pointers in linked lists", "input_sha256": "2d4cd832e51e7b84accb51b33cdbe69630c5b76dc17c0986f9fdaf9d6248b23b", "output_sha256": "430a369bd9d51303e497512b1d7eada81059e89a055e27cd943af954452bd079", "ttft_seconds": 0.7331724613904953, "elapsed_seconds": 7.688419386744499, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 38, "prompt_ms": 683.3, "prompt_per_token_ms": 17.982, "prompt_per_second": 55.6, "predicted_n": 256, "predicted_ms": 7004.0, "predicted_per_token_ms": 27.359, "predicted_per_second": 36.6, "draft_n": 267, "draft_n_accepted": 169}, "engine": {"generated": 256, "prompt_tokens": 38, "prompt_ms": 683.3, "decode_ms": 7004.0, "finish": "length", "drafts_accepted": 169, "drafts_offered": 267, "reused": 0, "hits": 169548, "lookups": 171360, "ram_blobs": 1309, "file_blobs": 0, "file_mb": 0.0, "prompt_read": 38, "offloaded": 0, "chunk": 0, "experts_streamed": 0}, "gpus": 2, "workers": 8, "profile": false, "aux_cpus": "off", "mode": "layer", "shared_stream": "default", "mtp": true, "max_drafts": 3, "draft_acceptance": 0.6329588014981273}
